It took me 2 years to get my first ascension. Now, just over 1 month later,
I've ascended again. I've always had a weak spot for dwarvish archeologists -- I
like to take all gems with me, and the thought of a dwarf with a huge pickaxe
killing everything in sight is just too funny. I also wanted to try a character
that could do a bit more spellcasting (previous ascension was a Valkyrie).

Some short remarks about the game:
    - The minetown temple was crossaligned... again! It's been that way for the
      last 15 games or so (probably more). Is this just bad luck, or is the
      chance of getting a coaligned altar smaller than 1/3?
    - In my games, gauntlets of power seem to be very common before the mines,
      and extremely rare thereafter. It makes fighting monsters a lot easier,
      you can eat what you want to get poison resistance :)
    - Only wishes were from the castle wand (0:2).
    - My brain got eaten in the wizards tower, so I was very happy that I
      could (still) cast identify and magic mapping.
    - I accidently vaporized my +6 silver sabre trying to enchant Grayswandir.
    - I crushed Arepo the tame Aleax under the drawbridge :'-(
    - Mysterious force was killing. The wizard showed op 8 times, so I guess I
      was thrown back 30 times, if not more. After going from completely full to
      hungry, I had gone up only 9 levels. Very frustrating.
    - On the astral plane, some rogue decided to zap 2 wands of death at me.
      He only managed to kill Famine twice. I never touched Famine, but he is
      still on my kill list. If my pet had killed him, I could understand this,
      but in this case, I really had nothing to do with it. Is this a bug or
      not?


